    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1360,
        800
      ],
      "size": [
        360,
        220
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 17,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "Use denoised_output here, not output",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### output vs denoised_output\n\nPass 1's sigma schedule (SplitSigmas high_sigmas) does NOT end at 0.0, so its `output` slot is divided by (1 - sigma[-1]) inside inverse_noise_scaling -- a no-op only when the schedule reaches 0, a ~13x blow-up here. `denoised_output` is the model's own clean-x0 estimate at every step and is valid regardless of where the schedule stops. Wire `denoised_output`, not `output`, out of ANY sampler whose schedule doesn't end at 0 -- confirmed the hard way: `output` here decodes to a uniform checkerboard of shuffled tiles, `denoised_output` decodes clean."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
